# Introduction to new components
## Breadboards
- What are they
- - Important prototyping tool that provides secure, but temporary connections between wires and components.
- I tend to describe it as "connect the dots" when using breadboards to describe how electrical connections can take multiple forms to complete a circuit.
- - How do the work? talk about the connected outer rails and interior connected columns
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breadboard#/media/File:Breadboard.png
- How are they useful for distributing power?
- How are they useful for connecting components
- Links
Breadboard Tutorials

SparkFun — How to Use a Breadboard
https://learn.sparkfun.com/tutorials/how-to-use-a-breadboard/all
Probably the gold standard beginner reference — covers internal connections, power rails, how rows and columns work, and builds up to a simple LED circuit with a button and resistor. SparkFun Learn This one is worth bookmarking for your students.
Science Buddies — How to Use a Breadboard
https://www.sciencebuddies.org/science-fair-projects/references/how-to-use-a-breadboard
Includes a tutorial video plus detailed text explanations, covers full-size vs. half-size vs. mini boards, and explains breadboard diagrams vs. schematics — written for true beginners with no assumed knowledge. Science Buddies
Build Electronic Circuits — Breadboard Beginner's Guide
https://www.build-electronic-circuits.com/breadboard/
Short and visual — explains horizontal vs. vertical connections, the center gap, power rail conventions, and walks through connecting an LED and resistor to a battery. Also has a quick intro video (~2:30). Build Electronic Circuits
Adafruit — Breadboards for Beginners (PDF)
https://cdn-learn.adafruit.com/downloads/pdf/breadboards-for-beginners.pdf
Shows what's physically inside a breadboard — the metal clips with teeth that grip component leads — which is great for helping students understand why connections work the way they do. Adafruit
Instructables — Breadboard Tutorial (7 Steps)
https://www.instructables.com/Breadboard-Tutorial/
Step-by-step format with video option, covers everything from the name's origin through to practical usage. Instructables
Starting Electronics — Building a Circuit on Breadboard
https://startingelectronics.org/beginners/start-electronics-now/tut1-breadboard-circuits/
Walks through building a simple LED circuit and then explains the internal connections with annotated photos showing exactly which strips are connected. Starting Electronics


