# Project 3 Workshop 1 : Prototype V1
## Overview
All workshops in project 3 will have the same 2 components: A current working prototype and a design sketch for the final version. Over the course of the 3 workshops you will be developing both aspects of the project.

## Working Prototype 1 - Control the rotation of the servo with light value
The goal is to create the most simple input/output connection between the sensor and the servo as a starting point. Follow the step by step guide that leads to the light sensor value controlling the servo rotation in realtime. The servo horn must have an additional object attached to it.
projects/03-LightAndLightness/classes/class09-LDR-to-Servo.md

## Project Design V1
In parallel to creating the first simple interaction, you should create a drawing that shows your intial concept for your project. Read the project brief carefully : https://canvascloud.ocadu.ca/courses/13538/pages/light-and-lightness . Yes, this is an early stage, but you will be improving it each week through iteration. The drawing should note
- General concept of the interaction : How is light being used to effect movement
- Position of Light Sensor
- Servo motor(s): what are they attached to and what do they do?
- Overall form factor and size: On a table, free standing, hanging, etc
- How is it being powered? 

## Submission
Create a post that shows
- Video of interaction between light sensor and servo
- Image of V1 of your design
- 1 - 2 sentence description of your design concept

